  "text_md": "3.000\n\n400\n\n80\n\n![](<027880a87e3c2ad4cf8c05f477597c0c6da7_page_6_pg1_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\n2,400\n\n60\n\n300\n\n2\n\n1\n\n1.800\n\n8\n\n40\n\n200\n\n2\n\n8\n\n1.200\n\n20\n\n100\n\n0.600\n\n0.000\n\n12\n\n16\n\n20\n\ntime (h)\n\n80\n\n4.00\n\n2\n\nB\n\n3.50\n\n60\n\n2.50\n\n40\n\n2.00\n\n1.50\n\n0.30\n\n1.00\n\n20\n\n0.20\n\n0.10\n\n0.50\n\n0.00\n\n0.00\n\n16\n\n20\n\ntime (h)\n\n0.200\n\n0.150\n\n0.100\n\n0.050\n\n6\n\n0.000\n\n0.20\n\n0.00\n\n0.10\n\n0.30\n\n(h ')\n\np\n\nFIG. 2. Growth of M. thermautotrophicus in a fed-batch reactor at high gassing rate. The organism was cultured in 2.5 liters of mineral medium at a constant gassing rate of 428 ml min   1 with 80% H 2 –20% CO 2 (vol/vol). Measurements started ( t   0 h) 8 h after adjustment of the gassing rate. Panels A to C and symbols are as described in the legend to Fig. 1.\n\ndissolved hydrogen partial pressure steadily decreased to become as low as 1 kPa. Before that time, the hydrogen consumption rate had become constant (84 mlmin ~ 1), and 989 of the gas ended up in methane. When the pH had reached the minimum at t = 10 h, the density increased linearly over time This period is denoted as the linear phase. Apparently, growth now became limited by the Hz supply. To test this; the organism was grown at higher gassing rate (428 ml min The same growth behavior was found (Fig: 2A). Quite remark ably, PHz did not to low values during the linear growth stage, but it was maintained as high hydrogen consumption rate became constant 275 ml min ~ 1), but the gas was only partly utilized. Further experiments showed that the pHz values could be manipulated by the optical drop (vHz gen mass transfer characteristics, gassing ratelculture volume ratio and mixing intensity (number of impellers), steady pHz values were obtained during the linear growth phase that ranged between 1 and 59 kPa. Linear growth could proceed for prolonged   periods of time (at least 72 h), at which ODgoo values of up to 7 to 10 were obtained (data not shown) drogen consumption and methane production rates; as well as dissolved hydrogen partial pressures, however, remained constant throughout the whole of linear growth. Hyperiod Growth rates; growth yields, and methane-forming activities in the fed-batch fermentor system. As noted above, three conexponential; and linear phases. The exponential phase is usually determined from the straight section of the graphs in which the (natural) logarithm of biomass (or OD) is plotted lag against\n\n",
